/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (By sharing the same underlying architecture for both text and audio, the model benefits from cross-modal knowledge transfer. Additionally, the attention mechanisms in the decoder can seamlessly integrate information from both text and audio sequences. Thus, we can implement a simple adjustment to convert a text-only model into one that processes both text and audio by enlarging the embeddings matrix M to be of size \(t + a\) x e, where a denotes the count of audio tokens)
/Alt ()
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
